Dav?

5
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:34,429
For my wife but not for our company, her love for her minions helped me to learn how to

6
00:00:34,429 --> 00:00:37,460
and the one most sure of success

7
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,810
for the young man starting in life

8
00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:41,390
is to select the vocation

9
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:44,649
which is most congenial to his tastes.

10
00:00:44,649 --> 00:00:47,609
Parents and guardians are often quite too negligent

11
00:00:47,609 --> 00:00:49,649
in regard to this.

12
00:00:49,649 --> 00:00:52,810
It's very common for a father to say,

13
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:56,170
for example, I have five boys.

14
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:58,090
I will make Billy a clergyman,

15
00:00:58,090 --> 00:00:59,490
John a lawyer,

16
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:00,770
Tom a doctor,

17
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,890
and Dick a farmer.

18
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:04,849
He then goes into town and looks about

19
00:01:04,849 --> 00:01:07,170
to see what he will do with Sammy.

20
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:11,230
He returns home and says, Sammy, I see watchmaking

21
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:13,189
as a nice, genteel business.

22
00:01:13,189 --> 00:01:15,659
I think I will make you a goldsmith.

23
00:01:15,659 --> 00:01:19,579
He does this, regardless of Sam's natural inclinations

24
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:21,049
or genius.

25
00:01:21,049 --> 00:01:25,650
We are all, no doubt, born for a wise purpose.

26
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:28,569
There is as much diversity in our brains

27
00:01:28,569 --> 00:01:30,519
as in our countenances.

28
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:33,250
Some are born natural mechanics,

29
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:36,560
while some have great aversion to machinery.

30
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,519
Let a dozen boys of 10 years get together,

31
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:42,920
and you will soon observe two or three are whittling

32
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:45,219
out some ingenious device,

33
00:01:45,219 --> 00:01:48,579
working with locks or complicated machinery.

34
00:01:48,579 --> 00:01:50,620
When they were but five years old,

35
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:54,079
their father could find no toy to please them like a puzzle.

36
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:56,379
They are natural mechanics,

37
00:01:56,379 --> 00:01:59,849
but the other eight or nine boys have different aptitudes.

38
00:01:59,849 --> 00:02:02,049
I belong to the latter class.

39
00:02:02,049 --> 00:02:04,810
I never had the slightest love for mechanism.

40
00:02:04,810 --> 00:02:08,199
On the contrary, I have a sort of abhorrence

41
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:10,139
for complicated machinery.

42
00:02:10,139 --> 00:02:14,349
I never had ingenuity enough to whittle a side or tap

43
00:02:14,349 --> 00:02:15,789
so it would not leak.

44
00:02:15,789 --> 00:02:18,349
I never could make a pen that I could write with

45
00:02:18,349 --> 00:02:21,370
or understand the principle of a steam engine.

46
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:24,150
If a man was to take such a boy as I was

47
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:26,469
and attempt to make a watchmaker of him,

48
00:02:26,469 --> 00:02:28,189
the boy might, after an apprenticeship

49
00:02:28,189 --> 00:02:31,469
of five or seven years, be able to take a part

50
00:02:31,469 --> 00:02:34,000
and put together a watch.

51
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,639
But all through life, he would be working uphill

52
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:40,889
and seizing every excuse for leaving his work

53
00:02:40,889 --> 00:02:43,120
and idling away his time.

54
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,979
Watchmaking is repulsive to him.

55
00:02:45,979 --> 00:02:48,960
Unless a man enters upon the vocation intended for him

56
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:53,240
by nature and best suited to his peculiar genius,

57
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,069
he cannot succeed.

58
00:02:55,069 --> 00:02:57,610
I am glad to believe that the majority of persons

59
00:02:57,610 --> 00:02:59,889
do find their right vocation,

60
00:02:59,889 --> 00:03:03,009
yet we see many who have mistaken their calling

61
00:03:03,009 --> 00:03:07,159
from the blacksmith up or down to the clergyman.

62
00:03:07,159 --> 00:03:12,400
You will see, for instance, that extraordinary linguist, the learned blacksmith, who ought

63
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:17,439
to have been a teacher of languages, and you may have seen lawyers, doctors, and clergymen

64
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:27,419
who were better fitted by nature for the anvil or the lapstone.

